# CVE-2025-64756 - glob CLI command injection [HISTORICAL EXAMPLE - RESOLVED]
# Affects: glob package (transitive dependency of Gemini CLI)
# Issue: Command injection via -c/--cmd flag with shell:true
# Risk: LOW - Requires explicit use of glob CLI with -c flag, which is rare in dev workflows
# Status: RESOLVED - Gemini CLI 0.17.0 upgraded to glob@12.0.0 (patched)
# Fixed Versions: glob@10.5.0+ and glob@11.1.0+
# Timeline:
#   - 2025-11-18: CVE added to ignore list (Gemini CLI 0.15.4 used vulnerable glob@10.4.5)
#   - 2025-11-20: Gemini CLI 0.17.0 released with glob@12.0.0
#   - 2025-11-21: Container updated to Gemini CLI 0.17.0, CVE removed
# Tracking:
#   - Monitor: https://www.npmjs.com/package/@google/gemini-cli
#   - Verify: npm view @google/gemini-cli@<version> dependencies.glob
# Review: Check for updates when new versions are released
# DO NOT UNCOMMENT - This is a resolved example for documentation purposes
# CVE-2025-64756

